notes=['# Change review comments — 25 September 2026','','Eleven review items resolved; one remains open for actual headset readability. Two mature chapters receive focused connections and orientation, three native photographs, and clearer invitations to their existing supporting works. No artifacts, roles, code excerpts or companion manuscripts removed.','','## What changes the reading','','The first hall asks what a reading keeps: a wide interval can report a fall while a nearby curve rises; a sum can retain a result and lose the climb. The second hall gives the next reading to the particle’s new address. Preserve that investigative thread. These edits repair the visitor’s route rather than impose another tutorial structure.','','The queue’s clock concern was already addressed by the previous Tiling ending. Its velocity-arrow sentence, however, would have introduced an error: the source estimates change per track angle and clamps the display length. Describe the timed puck and turning arrow without identifying length with speed.','','## Native photographs and checks','','15/15 Change_Intro checks and 12/12 Flow_Field checks pass; both final processes exit 0 with no GDScript errors. The probe loads the actual museum, exercises the authored control signals and keeps the current architecture, materials and nearby works. It does not replace a live museum bake. Existing renderer, UID and registry warnings remain in stdout logs. The initial field overview/report are retained in flow-first-view/; the second view moves the standing camera closer beside the canvas so its arrows and wrapping trails can be seen. Source screenshots remain unmodified.','','The introductory comparison uses the same camera before and after two STEP presses and revealing DERIVATIVE. The red sample stays at x = 1: h = 0.5 reports a negative rate; h = 0.125 reports a positive rate. The second comparison cycles RIGHT, LEFT, MID while retaining HOLD, then shows eight live intervals beside four held. The field starts held while particles move; FIELD TIME advances its time and can hold it again. These checks establish the supplied controls and state, not physical reach or tracked interaction.','','The two console close views and extracted strings are evidence for a later headset walk. No desktop photograph settles whether those figures are readable without leaning. Item 002 stays open. No arbitrary typography change was made.','','## Decisions','']
